<h1>Activities</h1>

<p>The Legion undertakes a wide range of activities, researching,
exploring, and reenacting many aspects of Roman life.  The choice of
activity is driven by the members' personal interests, with some
choosing to present a public display during our events.

<h2 class="project">Military Drills and Tactics</h2>

<p>The Imperial Roman army was an outstanding combat force.  It was
well trained, armed, and provisioned, but above all, operated using
group tactics, rather than as a collection of skilled (or less
skilled) individuals.

<p>Our <i>milites</i> (soldiers) train for and demonstrate Roman
marching drill (complete with Latin commands from the
<i>centurio</i>); use of weapons including the sword, shield, and
javelin; and combat formations for advancing under fire and attacks by
cavalry.


<h2 class="project">Food and Cooking</h2>

<p>Food was an important part of Roman life, from slaves to emperors.
From a basic <i>puls</i> porridge to the most elaborate feasts, there
was a massive variety in ingredients and preparation.  Some favourite
flavours are little used today, with the famous <i>garum</i> sauce no
longer popular and <i>silphium</i> now extinct.  On the other hand,
some ingredients are ubiquitous today, but were totally unknown in the
Roman Empire.

<p>See our display of Roman foods, learn about cooking and recipes,
and explore some unusual flavours.


<h2 class="project">Medical Treatments and Instruments</h2>

<p>Effective medical and surgical treatment often seems like a
relatively recent development, but the Roman <i>medicus</i> was
capable of suprisingly sophisticated treatment.  Our medicus displays
a range of Roman surgical instruments, both general purpose and highly
specialized, as well as treatments for a wide range of maladies.

<h2 class="project">Games and Gambling</h2>

<img class="project-left-image" src="images/legio-vi-games.jpg">

<p>Roman legionaries spent years deployed far from home, and when not
on duty, needed something to do!  Games and gambling were common
passtimes, but the games they played are quite different to those we
know today.  Some games reflect military tactics, others are
relatively simple, but regardless, you can learn the rules and play a
game or two against our experts!

